---
// /error-as-method/genealogy — the research direction, and how it developed.
//
// The line's genealogy is a single 1 600-line document that grew for thirty sessions. It opened
// with four stations of a historical argument, then split into three parallel tracks as the
// practice read further, and every extension is dated and attributed to the session that made
// it. That development is the most legible evidence this line has that it is research and not a
// series of pieces — and it was invisible, because the document rendered as one undifferentiated
// wall of markdown at the foot of the Atelier's works room.
//
// Nothing here is a summary. The stations, their years and their claims are the document's own
// headings; the addenda are its own dated section titles, in its own order. The full text stays
// where it is mirrored and is linked, not duplicated.
import Page from '@/layouts/Page.astro'
import SectionNav from '@/components/nightly/SectionNav.astro'
import { LINE_REPO } from '@/lib/engines/nightly-line'
import { addenda, stations, tracks } from '@/lib/nightly/apparatus'

const STATIONS = stations()
const ADDENDA = addenda()
const TRACKS = tracks()

const dated = ADDENDA.filter((a) => a.date)
const firstDate = dated[0]?.date
const lastDate = dated[dated.length - 1]?.date
const lastSession = ADDENDA[ADDENDA.length - 1]?.from
// Built as one string rather than a conditional element: an inline `{cond && <span>, …</span>}`
// left a stray space in front of the comma, because JSX keeps the whitespace around it.
const span = firstDate && lastDate ? `, ${firstDate} to ${lastDate}` : ''
---

<Page
  title="The genealogy — Error as Method | Frank Bültge"
  description="A genealogy of epistemic indifference: four historical stations that grew into three parallel tracks across thirty sessions, each extension dated by the night that made it."
>
  <main id="main" class="mx-auto w-full max-w-4xl flex-1 px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-fg-faint">
      <a href="/error-as-method" class="transition-colors hover:text-fg">Error as Method</a>
      <span> · the genealogy</span>
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-[clamp(28px,4.6vw,46px)] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em]">
      The Genealogy of Epistemic Indifference
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-fg-muted">
      The line's standing theoretical document. It opens on one question — <em>what is a machine's
      error, and who decides that?</em> — and answers it with a history rather than a definition:
      {STATIONS.length} stations across a century, describing not progress but a steady shift of the
      error out of the system and into the observer. It did not stay that way.
    </p>

    <SectionNav active="genealogy" />

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">The stations it was built on</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-fg-muted">
        The argument the genealogy was built on, in the document's own words. Each station names a
        text, a year, and what the error is <em>in</em> that text.
      </p>
      <ol class="mt-6 divide-y divide-line/60 border-y border-line/60">
        {
          STATIONS.map((station) => (
            <li class="grid gap-x-5 gap-y-1 py-4 sm:grid-cols-[2rem_10rem_1fr]">
              <span class="font-mono text-[11px] tabular-nums text-fg-faint">{station.n}</span>
              <span class="font-medium">
                {station.author}
                <span class="ml-2 font-mono text-[11px] tabular-nums text-fg-faint">{station.year}</span>
              </span>
              <span class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{station.claim}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </section>

    {
      TRACKS.length > 0 && (
        <section class="mt-14 border-t border-line/60 pt-8">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Then it grew tracks</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-fg-muted">
            The four stations turned out to be one line through a wider field, and the practice
            opened parallel tracks rather than forcing later reading into the original sequence.
            The weight below is how often each track is named in the document — a rough measure of
            where the work actually went, not a claim about which matters.
          </p>
          {/* Drawn as SVG, not as a span with an inline style attribute: this site's CSP drops
              those silently, so a computed width would render as a zero-width bar that still
              looked like a deliberate design. Geometry belongs in the geometry. */}
          <svg
            class="mt-6 w-full max-w-xl"
            viewBox={`0 0 320 ${TRACKS.length * 26}`}
            role="img"
            aria-label={`How often each track is named: ${TRACKS.map((t) => `${t.label}, ${t.mentions}`).join('; ')}`}
          >
            {
              TRACKS.map((track, i) => {
                const max = Math.max(...TRACKS.map((t) => t.mentions))
                const w = Math.round((track.mentions / max) * 210)
                return (
                  <g>
                    <text x="0" y={i * 26 + 14} class="tr-label">{track.label}</text>
                    <rect x="62" y={i * 26 + 5} width={w} height="10" class="tr-bar" />
                    <text x={62 + w + 6} y={i * 26 + 14} class="tr-count">{track.mentions}</text>
                  </g>
                )
              })
            }
          </svg>
        </section>
      )
    }

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-line/60 pt-8">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">The direction, developing</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-fg-muted">
        Every extension the document carries, in its own order — {ADDENDA.length} of them, from
        session {ADDENDA[0]?.from} to session {lastSession}{span}. This is the part a finished
        essay hides: a research direction is not announced, it accumulates, and each row below is
        a night that read something and had to change the argument to fit it.
      </p>
      <ol class="mt-6 divide-y divide-line/60 border-y border-line/60">
        {
          ADDENDA.map((addendum) => (
            <li class="grid gap-x-5 gap-y-1 py-3 sm:grid-cols-[4rem_6.5rem_1fr]">
              <span class="font-mono text-[11px] tabular-nums text-fg-faint">S{addendum.sessions}</span>
              <span class="font-mono text-[11px] tabular-nums text-fg-faint">{addendum.date || '—'}</span>
              <span class="text-sm leading-relaxed">{addendum.title}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-faint">
        Rows without a date are extensions the document titles by session alone. Nothing is
        selected or reordered here: this is every dated addendum the file carries, parsed from its
        own headings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-line/60 pt-8 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed">
      <p class="text-fg-faint">Where to read it whole</p>
      <p class="mt-2">
        <a href="/atelier/texts/genealogie/" class="underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-fg">
          the full text, mirrored verbatim →
        </a>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-1">
        <a href={`${LINE_REPO}/blob/main/works/genealogie.md`} rel="noopener" class="underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-fg">
          works/genealogie.md in the practice's repository ↗
        </a>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-fg-faint">
        Derived at build time from that file's own headings — stations, tracks and addenda are the
        document's, not this page's.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Page>

<style>
  /* One identity ink for the track bars — not a status palette. A track that is named less often
     is not a worse track, so nothing here encodes a judgement in colour. */
  .tr-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, monospace);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    fill: var(--color-fg-faint, currentColor);
  }
  .tr-count {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, monospace);
    font-size: 10px;
    fill: var(--color-fg-faint, currentColor);
  }
  .tr-bar { fill: var(--color-fg-muted, currentColor); opacity: 0.45; }
</style>
